    "VISUAL_NAME": "Waterfall",
    "SCHEMA_NAME": "FAM_ASSET_DISPOSAL_VALUE_WATERFALL",
    "SCHEMA_DESCR": "VIS_010 - Asset Disposal Value - Sale vs Scrap (Waterfall) for the Management Dashboard. Real data source: FAM_ASSET_DISPOSAL, which carries the exact figures the FRS asks for (DISPOSAL_TYPE = SALE/SCRAP, PROFIT_LOSS_ON_DISPOSAL = SALE_VALUE - NET_BOOK_VALUE_AS_ON_DISPOSAL, both computed on the transaction). No proxy needed. Category = DISPOSAL_TYPE, Value = SUM(PROFIT_LOSS_ON_DISPOSAL) per type; the Waterfall visual auto-appends a Total bridge bar (option showTotal=true). Criteria: financial_year (prompt, string 'YYYY-YY' e.g. '2026-27', default matches the dashboard's global FINANCIAL_YEAR default) is parsed in SQL into the Apr 1 - Mar 31 window via split_part(?.financial_year,'-',1); branch_code (prompt, like + '%' default with an F2 lookup to FAM_BRANCH_MASTER) filters on FAM_ASSET_REGISTER.BRANCH_CODE, which the Asset Transfer business rule keeps current (On Approve, the register's BRANCH_CODE is updated to the TO value), so no extra join to the transfer history is needed. Disposal rows are included unless STATUS='CANCELLED' (a cancelled disposal never happened, so it should not count); DRAFT/PENDING_APPROVAL/APPROVED are all included because in the current environment the only disposal on record is still DRAFT (Approve has not been run yet) - narrowing to APPROVED only would render an empty chart despite real disposal data existing. Drill-through to the Asset Register Report (R), filtered to disposed assets, is not wired here since that report is not yet a declared project object (matches the dashboard's own DASHBOARD_DESCR assumption for its other tiles).",
    "SCHEMA_TYPE": "S",
    "OUTPUT_TYPE": "JSON",
    "DATABASE_TYPE": "1",
